 To compare them under the same setting, we use the seeds released by SmartFuzz and run them with \griffin{} on all four target DBMSs, with the same DBMS versions, resource allocation, campaign duration, and coverage measurement as the other tools in RQ2. As shown in Table~III, Table~IV, and Figure~7 below, \tool{} covers 422,130 branches and detects 22 bugs in total, compared with 394,825 branches and 17 bugs for SmartFuzz, i.e., 7\% more branches and 5 more bugs. On Virtuoso, SmartFuzz achieves slightly higher coverage than \tool{}, and both detect 3 bugs.
 
